Closes #53.

This fix stays inside the 1.3 progressive-field architecture and addresses the production trace showing 563 perturbation tiles, 350 queued chunks, 21 Hz presentation and rectangular black in-fill around 10^6.

## Precision admission

- double-float direct is restored as a complete tier;
- perturbation is selected only when exact adjacent sample coordinates collapse in the double-float split, or measured tile health fails;
- being in double-float mode no longer forces a reference request;
- the local reference and tile-local repair path remains unchanged for tiles that genuinely require it.

## Spatial admission and scheduling

- coarse, intermediate and authoritative lattices are admitted one at a time;
- a finer level is created only after the current level drains and no newer camera request supersedes it;
- tile creation/clearing is processed in bounded 24-tile batches with event-loop yields;
- the full user iteration target remains attached to every tile and continues through bounded chunks.

## Monotonic presentation

- recurrence reset no longer binds or clears result/quality textures;
- direct and perturbation active, failure and unaccepted-cap paths leave prior accepted presentation untouched;
- coverage is monotonic, while authoritative `resolvedPixels` remains separate;
- direct-to-perturbation transitions and repair can no longer punch rectangular holes into the displayed field.

## Presentation load

- fully covered 2×2 child groups suppress their redundant parent draw;
- only admitted levels are protected from cache eviction, leaving a bounded history reserve during motion.

## Validation

- versioned as 1.3.1;
- CI checks lazy level admission, double-float distinguishability, monotonic coverage, recurrence-only reset, bounded creation batches and parent culling;
- no depth threshold, interaction iteration ceiling, scene-specific constant or viewport fallback is introduced.

