## Incident

The deployed SEC row-isolation repair reached ASML company evidence for CIK `0000937966` and exposed the complete malformed-row pattern: six consecutive invalid rows at indexes 585–590 in a 591-row SEC submissions set. The ordinary one-percent boundary allowed five, so the production cycle correctly remained fail-closed.

## Fix

- preserve the ordinary one-percent allowance for isolated, recent, scattered, or middle-of-history malformed rows;
- add a distinct policy only for filing histories with at least 100 rows where every malformed row forms one contiguous oldest-row suffix;
- bound that suffix at two percent and never more than ten rows;
- keep missing columns, misaligned parallel arrays, zero usable rows, scattered corruption, and over-cap suffixes fail-closed;
- record the suffix classification, applied boundary, indexes, CIK, and policy version without filing contents or credentials;
- add production-sized ASML regression coverage plus negative tests for scattered and over-cap corruption.

## Governance boundary

No SEC value or acceptance timestamp is inferred, repaired, or fabricated. No strategy, threshold, candidate authority, CIO authority, portfolio construction, execution, or live-money permission changes.

