## Outcome

Layer organization capacity detection and active-active AWS/Hetzner Linux runner capacity onto the bounded GHA continuity executor already merged in #610 and promoted to `dev` in #620.

This replacement deliberately preserves the existing `gha-clone-server-rs` workflow mirror. It adds a separate `gha-capacity-audit` binary and provider runner declarations instead of overwriting the merged executor.

## Changes

- pin the shared ARC controller and both scale-set charts to `0.14.2`;
- add manual-gated `sonus-ci` scale sets in AWS and Hetzner using the same scale-set name and distinct `sonus-aws` / `sonus-hetzner` runner groups;
- add a shared restricted namespace, ExternalSecret, resource quota/limits, and public-HTTPS-only NetworkPolicy;
- add `gha-capacity-audit`, which reads current-month organization Actions usage and budgets, emits a fail-closed capacity decision, and can optionally reconcile selected-repository routing variables;
- package both Rust binaries in one non-root immutable image;
- add a suspended, mutation-disabled capacity CronJob with an image-digest activation gate;
- add credential-free static contracts, legacy-scaffold compatibility, actionlint, and an opt-in read-only `sonus-ci` smoke;
- document activation, special-platform exclusions, rollback, and required evidence.

## Safety / activation gates

Nothing in this PR registers or routes production jobs automatically:

- provider scale-set Applications have no automated sync policy;
- the capacity CronJob is `suspend: true`;
- `GHA_CAPACITY_MUTATION_ENABLED=false`;
- the capacity image remains digest-gated;
- GitHub runner groups, App secrets, selected-repository access, AWS smoke, Hetzner smoke, provider-loss failover proof, and hosted-vs-ARC parity are all required before routing changes;
- public-fork, macOS/iOS, Windows, Android/KVM, privileged/socket, and production-deployment workloads remain outside the general Linux lane.

## Billing evidence

The repository connector cannot read the organization billing total, so this PR does not guess the current Sonus Auris minute count. The audit requires a GitHub App installation with organization Administration read permission. Variables write is only needed later for selected-repository routing mutation.

## Validation

Local credential-free contracts pass for:

- ARC/controller/runner version coherence;
- AWS/Hetzner active-active identity and manual gating;
- restricted pod, secret, resource, and network boundaries;
- billing API/routing/mutation contracts and unit-test presence;
- immutable two-binary image and suspended CronJob;
- workflow syntax inputs, docs, and credential-marker rejection.

GitHub Actions is expected to run rustfmt, Clippy, all Rust tests, both Sonus validators, actionlint, deployment/security contracts, and repository catalog checks on this branch.

